§ `Anti-social Behaviour, Crime and Policing Act 2014 — section 43 (record spelling)`

-- The SEMANTIC TWIN of `antisocial.l4`: the same section 43, the same decisions
-- under the same names, spelled with `DECLARE` records instead of top-level
-- `ASSUME`.
--
-- WHY IT EXISTS. `ASSUME` is uninterpreted, so `l4 run` cannot evaluate a
-- decision in `antisocial.l4`, and `lowerQuery` builds a scenario only out of a
-- record-literal query argument — an `#EVAL` there would lower to a query with
-- no facts at all. An ASSUME-shaped seed therefore ships no evaluable
-- directive, and pairing its zero oracles against its zero tests would be a
-- VACUOUS green: the tier-1 harness would report a pass having executed
-- nothing.
--
-- HOW IT ANCHORS THE OTHER FILE. Every record field below is named EXACTLY as
-- the corresponding `ASSUME` in `antisocial.l4` — character for character — and
-- every record is named exactly as the corresponding `ASSUME`d TYPE. The two
-- files therefore mangle to the SAME s(CASP) atoms at the SAME arities: a
-- boolean field reaches the Blawx leg through `RProj` + `RUnify TRUE` and is
-- collapsed by the boolean-projection peephole to the signed unary goal
-- `is_authorised(P)`, which is exactly what `` `is authorised` p `` lowers to on
-- the `ASSUME` side; a value field `conduct` and an `ASSUME`d `conduct` both
-- give `conduct(R,B)`.
--
-- So `etc/blawx-tier1-harness.py` runs each `#EVAL` below TWICE: once against
-- this file's own workspaces, and once with the same fact rows replayed against
-- `antisocial.l4`'s workspaces. The `-- L4 oracle ==>` value measured here is
-- the single expectation for both runs. No expectation is authored twice, and
-- none is hand-derived — which is what the P4 brief asks for, and the reason
-- the field names below must not be "tidied".
--
-- The declaration ORDER is load-bearing too, for a smaller reason: it is what
-- lets the two emitted ontologies be compared block for block rather than as
-- sets. Records are declared in the order the `ASSUME`d TYPEs appear in
-- `antisocial.l4`, and fields in the order the `ASSUME`s appear.
--
-- ONE THING THIS FILE CANNOT MIRROR: `antisocial.l4` carries an unreferenced
-- `ASSUME EffectTarget IS A TYPE` as the reachability gate's witness. A record
-- world has no equivalent — an unused `DECLARE` is dropped by a different
-- mechanism — so `effect_target` is simply absent from both goldens, for two
-- different reasons.
--
-- The grouping recorded in `antisocial.l4`'s header was measured on this
-- spelling; rows q10 and q11 below are the two discriminating scenarios that
-- pinned it, and they are kept for that purpose.

DECLARE Person HAS
    `is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Receiver HAS
    `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
    conduct IS A Behaviour

DECLARE Behaviour HAS
    effect IS A Consequence
    `is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Consequence HAS
    `is detrimental` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS A BOOLEAN
    `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Anti-social Behaviour, Crime and Policing Act 2014 s.43(1): an authorised person may issue a community protection notice to an individual aged 16 or over, or to a body, if satisfied on reasonable grounds that (a) the conduct of the individual or body is having a detrimental effect, of a persistent or continuing nature, on the quality of life of those in the locality, and (b) the conduct is unreasonable.
@ref https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2014/12/section/43
GIVEN p IS A Person
      r IS A Receiver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may issue a community protection notice` IF
        p's `is authorised`
    AND `the recipient is a person to whom a notice may be given` r
    AND `the conduct is having a detrimental effect of a persistent or continuing nature` r
    AND `the conduct is unreasonable` r

@export s.43(1): the notice may be given "to an individual aged 16 or over, or to a body". The two limbs are alternatives, and nothing else is a permissible recipient.
GIVEN r IS A Receiver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is a person to whom a notice may be given` IF
        r's `is an individual aged 16 or over`
     OR r's `is a body`

@export s.43(1)(a): the conduct of the individual or body "is having a detrimental effect, of a persistent or continuing nature, on the quality of life of those in the locality".
GIVEN r IS A Receiver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is having a detrimental effect of a persistent or continuing nature` IF
    `the effect is detrimental, persistent, and affects the quality of life in the locality` (r's conduct's effect)

@export s.43(1)(a), of the effect itself: it must be "detrimental", "of a persistent or continuing nature", and on "the quality of life of those in the locality" — all three, of the same effect.
GIVEN c IS A Consequence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the effect is detrimental, persistent, and affects the quality of life in the locality` IF
        c's `is detrimental`
    AND c's `is of a persistent or continuing nature`
    AND c's `affects the quality of life of those in the locality`

@export
@ref Anti-social Behaviour, Crime and Policing Act 2014, s.43(1)(b)
GIVEN r IS A Receiver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is unreasonable` IF
    r's conduct's `is unreasonable`

-- q1: an authorised person, an individual aged 16 or over, every limb of (a), and unreasonable conduct
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- q2: the issuer is not authorised
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS FALSE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q3: the recipient is a body rather than an individual -- s.43(1)'s second limb
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS FALSE,
                       `is a body` IS TRUE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- q4: neither an individual aged 16 or over nor a body
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS FALSE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q5: the effect is not detrimental
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS FALSE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q6: the effect is not of a persistent or continuing nature
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS FALSE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q7: the effect does not affect the quality of life of those in the locality
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS FALSE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q8: limb (b) fails -- the conduct is not unreasonable
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS FALSE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q9: an individual aged 16 or over who is also a body -- the OR is inclusive
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS TRUE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- q10 GROUPING PIN: not authorised, but a body with every other limb true.
-- Any reading that lets the OR escape its conjunct answers TRUE here.
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS FALSE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS FALSE,
                       `is a body` IS TRUE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q11 GROUPING PIN: an authorised individual with none of the conduct limbs.
-- Any reading that lets the OR escape its conjunct answers TRUE here.
#EVAL `may issue a community protection notice`
        (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS FALSE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS FALSE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS FALSE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS FALSE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q12: the recipient limb alone -- a body qualifies
#EVAL `the recipient is a person to whom a notice may be given`
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS FALSE,
                       `is a body` IS TRUE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS FALSE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS FALSE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS FALSE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS FALSE))
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- q13: the recipient limb alone -- neither limb holds
#EVAL `the recipient is a person to whom a notice may be given`
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS FALSE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q14: limb (a) of the effect itself -- all three properties
#EVAL `the effect is detrimental, persistent, and affects the quality of life in the locality`
        (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                          `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                          `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE)
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- q15: limb (a) of the effect itself -- detrimental and persistent, but not on the quality of life
#EVAL `the effect is detrimental, persistent, and affects the quality of life in the locality`
        (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                          `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                          `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS FALSE)
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q16: limb (b) alone, reached through the conduct chain
#EVAL `the conduct is unreasonable`
        (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                       `is a body` IS FALSE,
                       conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                              `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                  `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- q17: the #ASSERT path on the headline decision
#ASSERT `may issue a community protection notice`
            (Person WITH `is authorised` IS TRUE)
            (Receiver WITH `is an individual aged 16 or over` IS TRUE,
                           `is a body` IS FALSE,
                           conduct IS (Behaviour WITH effect IS (Consequence WITH `is detrimental` IS TRUE,
                                                                                  `is of a persistent or continuing nature` IS TRUE,
                                                                                  `affects the quality of life of those in the locality` IS TRUE),
                                                      `is unreasonable` IS TRUE))
-- L4 oracle ==> assertion satisfied
